   "p": "Look at the number, then at the noun's singular. Something is upside down."
  },
  {
   "rule": "From three to ten the number takes the <strong>opposite gender</strong> to the noun. With a masculine noun (<span class='ar'>طَالِبٌ</span>، <span class='ar'>كِتَابٌ</span>) the number has ة: <span class='ar'>ثَلَاثَةُ طُلَّابٍ</span>. With a feminine noun (<span class='ar'>طَالِبَةٌ</span>، <span class='ar'>سَاعَةٌ</span>) it drops the ة: <span class='ar'>ثَلَاثُ طَالِبَاتٍ</span>. The counted noun comes after it, plural and majrūr."
  },
